      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VR users don't have a crouch or prone button. I suspect all the crouch and prone buttons are doing on desktop is faking various tracked head heights behind the scenes?\n\nAnyway, since all we can do now is check how high their head tracking data is with GetTrackingData. You can kind of use that to tell if they are crouching.\n\nBut this doesn't account for avatar height, so...\n\nI propose we get something like vector3 VRCPlayerApi.GetDefaultViewpoint to get their's avatars view ball point ... the same vector3 for the viewball when uploading an avatar. Then you can compare it to their current head tracking data and tell how straight they are standing vs laying down, regardless of avatar size",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-10T22:10:47.639Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I want to get player status of crouching/prone or not.\nI want to use it in my UDON game world. For example, as a health point recovery action.\n\nSDK3/Udonでプレイヤーのしゃがみ/ほふく状態(isCrouch/isProne)が取得したいです。\n例えばゲームワールドでしゃがみで回復したりするアクションを取得する事を想定しています。",
